 ## Overview
-This method performs axis-aligned volume rendering by decomposing a 3D scalar dataset across multiple MPI processes, where each process renders a spatial subdomain by casting rays along the projection axis (typically Z) and compositing front-to-back [S1, S3, unofficial]. It differs from global ray casting by distributing data spatially along the view axis rather than distributing rays, which eliminates per-ray communication overhead and enables independent compositing per process [S2, unofficial]. The method supports 1D (x-axis) and 2D (x and y axes) data decomposition to balance load and memory usage [S3, unofficial].
